{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.nonzero_cluster_needs_second_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.nonzero_cluster_needs_second_bond","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L144-L157","doc":"**A nonzero μ₃ door forces a genuinely present second bond.**  If\n`secondDiff g₀ gₐ g_b gₐᵦ ≠ 0` then the configuration is *not* single-bond:\n`g_b ≠ g₀ ∨ gₐᵦ ≠ gₐ`.  Contrapositive of `secondDiff_single_bond_vanishes`\nlifted to arbitrary second-bond values — the μ₃ mechanism is exclusive to\nA ≥ 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.deuteron_content_is_first_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.deuteron_content_is_first_order","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L123-L136","doc":"**The deuteron's binding content is entirely FIRST-order.**  Specialising the\ndecomposition to a single-bond configuration (`g_b = g_∅`, `g_ab = g_a`): the\ntotal change equals `firstDiff g₀ gₐ` alone — the second-order (μ₃) and the\nabsent-bond first-order terms both vanish.  Hence the deuteron magnitude is\ncarried by the bare per-bond amplitude `Δ¹g`, and any deficit in it (the 5.853×)\n**cannot** be recovered from cluster structure, which is empty here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.total_change_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.total_change_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L111-L121","doc":"**Möbius / inclusion decomposition of the total two-bond change.**  The full\nchange of the joint block-trace from the empty configuration to both bonds\npresent decomposes exactly into the two first-order (single-bond) terms plus the\none second-order (3-body) term:\n\n    g_ab − g_∅ = Δ¹g_a + Δ¹g_b + Δ²g.\n\nThis is the finite Möbius inversion on the Boolean lattice `{∅, a, b, ab}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.cluster3_single_bond_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.cluster3_single_bond_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**The μ₃ cluster is identically zero at A = 2.**  Consequently\n`c₃ = −E₀·Δ²g = 0` for the deuteron for **every** `E₀`: the connected-3-body /\nsubmodularity mechanism cannot contribute to the single-bond binding magnitude.\nThis is the scope-(b) structural negative on the owner-suggested route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.secondDiff_single_bond_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.secondDiff_single_bond_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L91-L99","doc":"**A single-bond (deuteron) configuration** is one where the second interface\nbond `b` is absent, encoded by \"adding `b` changes nothing\":\n`g_b = g_∅` and `g_ab = g_a`.  Under this the **second mixed difference vanishes\nidentically**.  The μ₃ submodularity door therefore supplies *nothing* to a\nsingle-bond object — regardless of the (unknown, possibly submodular) sign of\nthe joint trace, because there is no second bond for it to act on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.cluster3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.cluster3","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L85-L87","doc":"The connected 3-body cluster `c₃ = −E₀·Δ²g` (matches\n`Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster3`, sign convention `E₀·(gₐ + g_b − g₀ − gₐᵦ)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.secondDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.secondDiff","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L80-L83","doc":"**Second mixed difference** (connected 3-body Ursell term / the μ₃ door):\n`Δ²g = g_ab − g_a − g_b + g_∅`.  `Δ²g < 0` is submodularity (the μ₃ > 0 door);\n`Δ²g > 0` is supermodularity (door shut). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.firstDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.firstDiff","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronFirstOrderCluster.lean#L75-L78","doc":"**First mixed difference** (connected 2-body / single-bond Ursell term):\n`Δ¹g = g_a − g_∅`.  This is the *whole* cluster content of a single bond — the\ndeuteron's honest binding object. ","signatureChunk":0}]}